# docs/ and scripts/ live at the repository root, and setup.py copies them
# into the package at build time so `shamway docs` and `shamway script` work
# from a wheel. Both halves of that need saying here.
#
# Graft the roots: `uv build` builds the wheel from the sdist, and without the
# sources in it setup.py's staging step finds no docs/ and no scripts/, skips
# silently, and the wheel ships whatever was already staged in the working
# tree. That is how a build published documentation and an installer older
# than the tree it was cut from.
graft docs
graft scripts

# Prune the staged copies: they are build output, regenerated on every build
# from the grafted originals above. Shipping them in the sdist is what let a
# stale one survive into the next wheel.
prune src/sevendtd_asset_pipeline/docs
prune src/sevendtd_asset_pipeline/scripts

global-exclude *.py[cod] __pycache__/*
